UID:GA-2026-11-03@ustaxsale
DTSTAMP:20261018T130819Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Georgia: statutory sale date (First Tuesday of the month\, 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\, at the courthouse)
DESCRIPTION:Tax deeds sold on the courthouse steps the first Tuesday of the month\; 12-month redemption with a 20% penalty.
URL:https://shamarrobinson.github.io/us-tax-sale-dashboard/#ga
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:TX-2026-11-03@ustaxsale
DTSTAMP:20261018T130819Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Texas: statutory sale date (First Tuesday of the month\, 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\, at the courthouse or designated venue)
DESCRIPTION:Sheriff or Constable sales the first Tuesday of the month\; 2-year redemption for homesteads and farmland (25%/50% penalty)\, 180 days for the rest.
URL:https://shamarrobinson.github.io/us-tax-sale-dashboard/#tx
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ND-2026-11-17@ustaxsale
DTSTAMP:20261018T130819Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:North Dakota: statutory sale date (Third Tuesday in November)
DESCRIPTION:The county takes a tax deed after 3 years and sells the parcels at an annual sale the third Tuesday in November.
URL:https://shamarrobinson.github.io/us-tax-sale-dashboard/#nd
END:VEVENT
